Z||000000||chester||12-03-2001||08:52 PM||||Here goes attempt two at this post  !!!!Cliff – I only attached four pictures but it said I have exceeded the limit of 8 ???  So I lost my whole post L. !!!!<P>Anyway, those who know me have heard the story about my Carlisle suspension fiasco.  To make a long story short my “new used” suspension broke an upper control arm a few miles away from home.  Did I say few, oh I meant FEW HUNDERED!  Needless to say I had to get home so I had Fred at the Petro truck stop tack weld it together.  Well being that I didn’t want to miss what turned out to be a killer show season, I continued to drive the car from show to show with the suspension welded back together.  Well, some time has passed since the last show and my car has been sitting on jack stands since.  Until this last weekend that is.  With a little nudge from my wife (thanks for the ratchet wrenches babe  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> ) and a blessing from mother nature (70+ on Saturday) I decided to finally replace the wasted suspension components.  Did I mention the bottom out at 90 plus?  Started at 7:00 and by 5:00 this is what I had.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Suspension.jpg"> <P><BR>So what do you think?  Replaced the RCC coilovers and installed the Street Dreams drop spindles that I bought over a year ago  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> .  Anyway, so the tires go on and this is what we get.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/lowered_right.jpg"> <P>How low can you go  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/lowered_left.jpg"> <BR><P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigline.jpg">     <BR>Modified 2.8<BR>2.5" Drop<BR>11" Brakes<BR>17" Revolutions<BR>RCC Coilover Suspension||||reg||1
Z||000001||chester||12-03-2001||08:53 PM||||I loved the look but way to low to be practical.  That was with the coilovers cranked up    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> ! So back to the factory spindles we go.  Here is my son pitching in for some brownie points.  He loves the test drives when were done    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/robbie_2.jpg"> <P>So, if my wife don’t claim them, I might have a set of Street Dreams drop spindles for sale.  Watch the mall forum!  Final ride height pics to follow soon!<P><BR>[This message has been edited by chester (edited 12-03-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by chester (edited 12-03-2001).]||||reg||1
